Vikram and Betal: The Wise Choice (Raw Story)

id: WBX_100147

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a boy who had to choose between two paths,” said Betal. “One path was easy but led to trouble. The other was difficult but led to success.”

The boy thought carefully.

His friends told him to choose the easy path.

But the boy remembered his father’s advice: “Always choose what is right, not what is easy.”

He chose the difficult path.

At first, it was hard.

But over time, he learned many things and became successful.

Those who chose the easy path faced problems later.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why did the boy succeed?”

Vikram replied, “Because he chose the right path instead of the easy one.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Always choose what is right, not what is easy.
